        ":question/problem": "Express $-\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&-\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{6}{5}\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{5}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{3}{5}\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right)-1\\right)&=\\frac{3}{5}\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
